            <history xml:id="history_idac784a4d">
               <p xml:id="idm101">Another translation which Scheibe was commissioned to carry out while living in Sønderborg was part of the complete sermons of the bishop, <persName xml:id="idm102" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Peder Hersleb</persName>. Scheibe worked on the three last volumes suggesting that he took over the job from the previous translator who was <persName xml:id="idm103" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johan Samuel Augustin</persName>. As was Scheibe’s usual practice, he included a foreword (though only in the second of the three volumes) summarising the sermons of the volume; furthermore, Scheibe added a few comments regarding the translation throughout the three volumes which appeared during the years 1752–57. The name of the translator does not appear in the volumes but is mentioned in Scheibe's biography of 1759 as being among those translations which he at that time had carried out for the publisher.</p>
            </history>
